---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = '2026-06-22';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Service — 24Observe"
  description="Plain-English terms for using 24observe — monitoring, logs, SIEM, and the AI SOC analyst. No surprises, no liability traps, no hidden billing."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px;">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="bar"></span> Legal · last updated {updated}</div>
      <h1 class="h1">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        These terms govern your use of 24observe (the "Service") operated by the maintainers of
        <a href="https://github.com/vikasswaminh/observe24">github.com/vikasswaminh/observe24</a>.
        By creating an account or self-hosting the Service, you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 56px;">1. The Service</h2>
      <p>
        24observe is an observability and security platform. It includes synthetic and uptime
        monitoring; log, metric, and trace ingestion with search; a SIEM with detections, correlation,
        and threat-intel enrichment; an AI SOC analyst that triages incidents; an operational context
        graph; and a programmable API/agent surface. We process the telemetry and configuration you send
        us, store the results, and notify or act per your configuration. Both a hosted SaaS at
        <code class="inline-code">api.24observe.com</code> and a self-hostable open-source distribution
        are offered under the same brand. These terms apply to the hosted SaaS only — the self-hosted
        distribution is provided under its own distribution terms; <a href="/contact">contact us</a> for details.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some features rely on third-party model providers (the AI analyst and AI-assisted configuration).
        Those run at config or incident time on redacted inputs; outputs are assistive and you remain
        responsible for verifying them before acting.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">2. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree NOT to:</p>
      <ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
        <li>Monitor URLs, hosts, or services you do not own or have explicit authorization to monitor.</li>
        <li>Use the Service to scan for vulnerabilities, brute-force credentials, or otherwise attack third parties.</li>
        <li>Configure check intervals or volumes designed to overwhelm a target (we cap intervals per plan;
          chained accounts to bypass these caps will be terminated).</li>
        <li>Store secrets, PII, or regulated data in monitor names, URLs, or webhook bodies. Headers are encrypted
          at rest; the rest is not.</li>
        <li>Resell, sublicense, or white-label the hosted Service. (You may freely fork the OSS distribution.)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This is a summary; our full <a href="/legal/acceptable-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a> governs in
        detail. We may suspend or terminate any account that violates it without notice, and will refund
        any unused prepaid balance on a good-faith termination that isn't for serious abuse.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">3. Plans, billing &amp; usage</h2>
      <p>
        We offer a Free plan and paid monthly plans (Team, Business, Scale). Paid plans are recurring
        subscriptions billed in advance through our payment provider, Dodo Payments; we don't store your
        card details. Each plan includes monthly allowances (e.g. monitors, log volume, AI investigations,
        connected endpoints) shown on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Log ingestion above your plan's included allowance is billed as <b>usage-based metered charges</b>
        at the per-GB rate on the pricing page; other allowances are enforced as caps (an HTTP 429 — they
        do not silently auto-upgrade you). You can cancel, change plan, or update payment any time from the
        in-product billing portal. Cancellation, refunds, downgrades, and failed-payment handling are
        governed by our <a href="/legal/refunds">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">4. Data ownership</h2>
      <p>
        You own the monitor configs and check-result data in your account. We make no claim to it.
        You can export it at any time via the API. On account deletion, all of your data is purged
        within 30 days from production and within 90 days from backups.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">5. Uptime &amp; SLA</h2>
      <p>
        We target 99.9% monthly availability for the hosted Service. There is no formal SLA credit on the
        free or paid plans today — if you need a contractual SLA, self-host or contact us about an
        enterprise tier (not yet generally available).
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">6. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided "as is." Our total liability for any claim is capped at the greater of (a) what
        you paid us in the preceding 12 months and (b) US$50. We are not liable for missed alerts, false alerts,
        downstream consequential damages, or anything covered by force majeure (provider outages, regional
        network failures, etc.). <b>Treat 24observe as a best-effort second pair of eyes — not as your only
        layer of monitoring.</b>
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">7. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        Either side may terminate at any time. You can delete your account from the dashboard. We may
        terminate for breach of section 2, non-payment, or to discontinue the Service entirely (with
        ≥30 days notice + data export window).
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We will email account owners ≥30 days before a material change to these terms. Continued use after
        the effective date constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href="mailto:support@24observe.com">support@24observe.com</a>.
        Security disclosures: <a href="mailto:security@24observe.com">security@24observe.com</a>
        (see <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">/.well-known/security.txt</a>).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
